# L §5.7: "`x in K` tests membership of a kind whose memberships aren't dated (a base kind and its parents);
# `x in K on d` tests membership on day d, for any kind, plain kinds with dated memberships included."  broker is
# a member of the plain kind wrapped from 2024 (a dated membership): `broker in wrapped` without `on` has no
# meaning, found at the key (RUN-DOMAIN, L §8.4); `broker in wrapped on 2026-06-30` is true.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind brokerages: place PLN min 0
kind wrapped

def w[x in brokerages]: bool = x in wrapped at reader

version v
  cite s
  known 2026-01-01
  brokerages + [broker] lives 2021-03-01..
  wrapped + [broker] lives 2024-01-01..

ask q1: w[broker] law 2026-06-30
ask q2: (broker in wrapped on 2026-06-30)
=== expect
q1: refused: RUN-DOMAIN ...
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q2: true
  cut 2026-12-31
